# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Python / editor
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- run output
# Every log and every benchmark/pipeline results tree is regenerated by the run
# that writes it.  `core.bench` and `core.pipeline` are resumable: their caches
# are keyed on a SHA-1 over the config AND the live backend set, so a stale
# cache is never silently reused.
*.log
# (verify/equiv_*.log were tracked by oversight until the 2026-09-09 clean: they are
#  the redirect targets of verify/run_equiv.sh and nothing reads them.)
bench_results/*
core_cache/
# ...except the golden reference results, which ARE committed on purpose: they are
# what the equivalence tests compare against, so an ignore rule must not silently
# swallow a new one.  `git add` on anything else under bench_results/ is a mistake.
!bench_results/baseline_tuning126.json
!bench_results/worker_sweep_smoke24.json
!bench_results/sweep_smoke24_*.json
!bench_results/optimised_tuning126_w4.json
!bench_results/equivalence_tuning126.json
!bench_results/feasibility_bound.json
!bench_results/recon_library_saturation.json
!bench_results/recon_hazards.json
!bench_results/fourcomponent_tuning126_w8.json
!bench_results/optimised_tuning126_w8.json
!bench_results/compare_tuning126.json
!bench_results/ambergate_smoke24_w8_a*.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- structure corpora
# NOT in git and deliberately so: about 6 GB of PDB files.  `pdbs/` (61 structures,
# 30 MB) IS tracked -- it is the reporting set `core.data.load()` reads and
# tests/test_geometry.py parses.  The two below are the extended corpora, rebuilt by
# re-running the RCSB queries.  Those fetch scripts were deleted in commit 1043d79
# and live in history:
#     git show 1043d79^:work/rcsb_query.py   # monomer query -> work/rcsb_ids.json
#     git show 1043d79^:work/download.py     # ids -> pdbs_ext/
#     git show 1043d79^:work/rcsb_prot.py    # protein query -> work/prot_ids.json
#     git show 1043d79^:work/dl_prot.py      # ids -> prots/
pdbs_ext/
prots/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- derived banks
# Large, and each is rebuilt on demand by the module named in the comment above it.
# esm_features.compute -- 1.5 GB
esm_cache.npz
# esm_features -- the PCA projection of the bank, and the per-target hot subset
esm_pca.npz
esm_small.npz
# core.data / peptide_db.build
peptide_db.npz
# fragment_db.build, and its wide variant
fragment_db.npz
fragment_db_large.npz

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- model checkpoints
# Trained per fold by the module named beside each.  Retraining is minutes to hours.
# The folds are pinned in peptide_folds.json, so a checkpoint is valid only for the
# fold definition committed alongside it -- see docs/FINDINGS.md, "Folds and clusters are
# pinned": correcting the identity clustering once silently moved 13 benchmark
# targets and invalidated every fold model.
# distogram.train_fold / core.predict.train_fold
distogram_models/
distogram_models_large/
# pairnet.train_fold
pairnet_models/
pairnet_models_large/
invfold_models/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- sprint-package caches
# What is left of s5/, s7/, s8/ and s9/ is the reference implementation the consolidated
# `core` package is measured against (see README).  These are its per-target caches:
# large, regenerable by the stage that writes them, and read by tests/ when present --
# tests/test_pipeline.py reads s9/final_cache READ ONLY and skips if it is absent, and
# tests/test_{data,geometry}.py do the same for s8/generate_univ and s8/consensus2_cache.
s5/esm32.npz
s5/esmraw.npz
s5/torsion_models/
s7/debias_cache/
s7/poolsize_cache/
s7/repr_cache/
s8/consensus2_cache/
s8/generate_univ/
s8/generate_rama.npz
s8/integrate_dmat/
s9/final_cache/
s9/synth_cache/*
# ...except the 126 per-target records that are the SOLE SOURCE of four 126-target
# golden constants (rmsd_avg 3.048338093879532 and the single-start fit 3.2005 both
# recompute from them exactly). Their writer s9/synth.py was deleted in d182738 and
# this directory was gitignored, so until now they existed in exactly one place on
# one disk. tests/test_equivalence.py and verify/headline_audit.py read them by glob,
# and SKIP rather than fail when they are absent -- the suite goes green as the
# evidence disappears. 2.0 MB is cheap insurance against that.
!s9/synth_cache/full_sc_75_*.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- consolidation 2026-09-04
# Untracked archive: Sprint 5-9 console logs moved out of s5/ s7/ s8/ s9/ so those package
# directories show only their tracked contents. Nothing was deleted -- see _archive/README.txt.
_archive/
# The pre-fold-repin distogram models, quarantined by rename so FRAG_LARGE=1 fails loudly
# instead of silently loading a model that may have trained on the target. See
# bench_results/recon_hazards.json item H1.
distogram_models_large.STALE-PRE-FOLD-REPIN-DO-NOT-USE/

*.npz
*/libcache/*

# The Sprint 12 containment-freshness corpus, 146 RCSB downloads. Same rule as pdbs_ext/
# and prots/ above: rebuilt by re-running the fetch, and the sprint's results are committed.
#     python -m s12.coord_benchN fetch
s12/newpdbs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- sprint caches
# Per-target memoisation written by the sprint that reads it, keyed on target and
# parameters. Same rule as s7/ s8/ s9/ above; these five were tracked by oversight.
s12/cache/
s13/cache/
s14/cache/
s15/cache/
s16/cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- results lab build
# Generated by s25/resultslab/build.py from results/structures + results/summary.
# structures.js alone re-embeds every PDB in results/structures/.
results/site/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- S26: the AMBER single-point cache
# 126 files, 1.5 MB, 63,000 genuine ff14SB/GBn2 single points (a serialised OpenMM run) whose only
# copy was this disk. Caught by the blanket *.npz rule above and never tracked (S25 L13, S26
# operational item 1). Whitelisted here, after the blanket rule, so it is committed.
!s24/cache_amber/*.npz

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- S26 governor runtime
# s26/governor.py keeps its live state here; the log IS a deliverable and is whitelisted.
s26/jobs/
s26/jobs_done/
s26/queue/
s26/queue_launched/
s26/logs/
s26/governor_state.json
s26/governor_state.json.tmp
!s26/governor.log

# S26 operational item 2: the transcript of the repaired verify/run_equiv2.sh run (four arms of
# smoke8: legacy baseline, project_grad = exact / fd / analytic) is a deliverable, so it is
# whitelisted past the blanket *.log rule above. The per-arm verify/e2_*.log files stay ignored.
!s26/results/run_equiv2.log
